# X4 (optional): the same four users in both start orders (the permuted plan: forward is the X2 concurrent arm, reverse puts the long
# users in segments 0-1 and slots 0-1 and the short ones in rows 32-63), 1,024 tokens each. The plan runs no solo arm: the gate
# compares each user across the two orders, and the texts are judged offline against the solo texts of S3a (the prompt sha256 values
# are identical, and the first 512 tokens of these answers are what S3a compared). After the fix the two orders must agree with each
# other and with solo for every user: the row and slot of a user no longer matter.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card exactness window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/exact and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image X0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; two concurrent arms at 1,024 tokens, each an engine build (10-30 min) plus its streams (up to 60
# min): 45-130 min (the gate budgets itself against the step limit, 380 min). Run after every stop job has passed.
# Stop rule (optional): strict. A divergence here that X2 did not show is a position effect, not the reduction order: read the divergence
# records segment and slot before anything else.
# Proves: position invariance of the packed route (segment, slot and extent) on real text.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-exact-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=permuted
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=1024
C2_GATE_JIT=record
